2026-09-25T18:28:06+00:00  tick W76 advanced -- "W76 decomposition (read-only while Δ runs; Δ peak flat at 5.66 GB). Every position is a UNIFORM multiple: glyph i at x0 + i*advanceCells (cols+1). Four consumers assume it: textCells (scroll length), root.charAdvance (scroll anim + tapAt hit-test), the series gauge (run.start*advanceCells, :489), the backdrop width. So W76 = (1) ONE offsets[] (cumulative x per char) computed at paint time by the closed loop: per adjacent pair, sample both glyphs through the aperture coverage; while they bleed, offsets[j>i] += 1 backdrop step; cap. (2) EVERY consumer reads offsets[] — tapAt by search, not division; scroll length = offsets[n]. (3) pixel gate: no adjacent pair bleeds (regular + bold) and a tap on char k resolves to k. Next step: the pure JS (bleed test + loop) in marquee-body.js, harness-tested like ringNext."
